{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130937-help-fall-of-the-camarilla-chronicles","id":1130937,"title":"Help Fall of the Camarilla Chronicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-18T13:04:46-07:00","id":1130937,"title":"Help Fall of the Camarilla Chronicles","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I'm carring on Fall of the Camarilla Chronicles. I'm at the point where of the Barbarian Invasion. <br /> The problem is that the PCs will be aware of the incoming army and about the delegation sent to parly with the barbarian king and I'm wondering how this event (a central one for the entire chronicle that MUST happpens) couldn't be stopped or prevented by a characters intervent.<br /> I mean: probably characters would like to intercept the army (obfuscated, as animals and so on), meet the king in its tent and blood bond, dominate him or simply kill him or a lot of other options that disciplines can easily allow. <br /> I have some rude idea of how to prevent this (maybe he could be possessed by a strix with the power that let the mind controls fail) but I would like to have other options from you and maybe make the things more interesting. <br /> <br /> Ps: I'm using 2ed mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T13:51:53-07:00","id":1130958,"title":"","content":"How exactly is one coterie, even a powerful one, going to stop an army capable of sacking the largest city in the world? They can kill the king, sure, but that'll do nothing to halt the massive tide of warriors falling upon Rome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T14:10:27-07:00","id":1130967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130937-help-fall-of-the-camarilla-chronicles?p=1130958#post1130958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How exactly is one coterie, even a powerful one, going to stop an army capable of sacking the largest city in the world? They can kill the king, sure, but that'll do nothing to halt the massive tide of warriors falling upon Rome.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said: <br /> <br /> Vinculum and order the king to retire its army<br /> <br /> Dominate 3: accept the compromise with the roman ambassy when they will come.<br /> <br /> Dominate 4: changing its memory letting him belive that he had agreed the compromise in exchange of a great reward. Or changing the memory in other infinite ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-18-2017, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T15:24:35-07:00","id":1130988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130937-help-fall-of-the-camarilla-chronicles?p=1130967#post1130967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I said: <br /> <br /> Vinculum and order the king to retire its army<br /> <br /> Dominate 3: accept the compromise with the roman ambassy when they will come.<br /> <br /> Dominate 4: changing its memory letting him belive that he had agreed the compromise in exchange of a great reward. Or changing the memory in other infinite ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Turn it around on the players: <br /> <br /> &quot;We know how history turns out; Rome is sacked, whether we like it or not. So why don't you tell me how you fail to prevent the invasion, how the city falls despite your best efforts?&quot; <br /> <br /> Alternatively, you can say fuck it and jump the rails. Our world doesn't have vampires in it, so maybe in the Chronicles of Darkness setting Rome survived further than it did in ours. Play to find out what happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T18:34:54-07:00","id":1131051,"title":"","content":"Remember that King Alaric wasn't an absolute ruler. Why would his warriors obey him if he couldn't give a good excuse for why he wouldn't sack the city? A Germanic King was an elected position (or at least a first among equals of the powerful warlords), and he rules so long as the warriors respect him. A sudden about-turn would require at least a convincing speech, and some way to convince the army that they'd be better off doing something. If you're not paying them off, all you do is put it off for a year. Once they realize that Alaric tricked them and no tribute is coming, they'll be on their way back under a new leader to sack Rome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:20:16-07:00","id":1131070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130937-help-fall-of-the-camarilla-chronicles?p=1131051#post1131051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that King Alaric wasn't an absolute ruler. Why would his warriors obey him if he couldn't give a good excuse for why he wouldn't sack the city? A Germanic King was an elected position (or at least a first among equals of the powerful warlords), and he rules so long as the warriors respect him. A sudden about-turn would require at least a convincing speech, and some way to convince the army that they'd be better off doing something. If you're not paying them off, all you do is put it off for a year. Once they realize that Alaric tricked them and no tribute is coming, they'll be on their way back under a new leader to sack Rome.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the big thing for me; if a barbarian host is gathered and near enough that a delegation is being sent... they're not going to turn back if their leader tells them too, because they've already come too far. They'd likely kill him for his cowardice and continue on their merry way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:12:06-07:00","id":1132263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130937-help-fall-of-the-camarilla-chronicles?p=1131070#post1131070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's the big thing for me; if a barbarian host is gathered and near enough that a delegation is being sent... they're not going to turn back if their leader tells them too, because they've already come too far. They'd likely kill him for his cowardice and continue on their merry way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And the players, too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4030-alexs","name":"AlexS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:55:44-07:00","id":1132295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130937-help-fall-of-the-camarilla-chronicles#post1130937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello,<br /> <br /> I'm carring on Fall of the Camarilla Chronicles. I'm at the point where of the Barbarian Invasion.<br /> The problem is that the PCs will be aware of the incoming army and about the delegation sent to parly with the barbarian king and I'm wondering how this event (a central one for the entire chronicle that MUST happpens) couldn't be stopped or prevented by a characters intervent.<br /> I mean: probably characters would like to intercept the army (obfuscated, as animals and so on), meet the king in its tent and blood bond, dominate him or simply kill him or a lot of other options that disciplines can easily allow.<br /> I have some rude idea of how to prevent this (maybe he could be possessed by a strix with the power that let the mind controls fail) but I would like to have other options from you and maybe make the things more interesting.<br /> <br /> Ps: I'm using 2ed mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember it right, there were vampires hidden in the army as well. Probably some of them can notice the characters trying to sneak in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T13:15:35-07:00","id":1132370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Max Deltree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1130937-help-fall-of-the-camarilla-chronicles?p=1132295#post1132295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I remember it right, there were vampires hidden in the army as well. Probably some of them can notice the characters trying to sneak in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a good point. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}